Hindsight and Obsidian are complementary. Don’t duplicate.

If Hindsight isn’t set up: `pip install hindsight-cursor` && `hindsight-cursor init` — official plugin only. Docs: https://hindsight.vectorize.io/sdks/integrations/cursor

## Routing (one line)

Agenda / working set → `wiki/hot.md`. Sticky agent facts (prefs, decisions, corrections) → Hindsight. Durable knowledge → wiki.

## Hindsight

Short facts across sessions (hooks + MCP): decisions, prefs, project context, corrections. Associative recall / consolidation / inceptions — not a second wiki.

- `sessionStart` → recall
- `stop` / `sessionEnd` → retain
- Mid-session: `recall` / `retain` / `reflect` when useful — not every turn

Config: `~/.hindsight/cursor.json`. Daemon: `http://127.0.0.1:9077`, bank `cursor`.

## Obsidian

Long notes under `obsidian/{{PROJECT}}/`. Follow `AGENTS.md`.

`hot.md` is the vault’s current focus (now / next / open threads). Rewrite it; don’t treat it as memory.

## Rules of thumb

- No full wiki pages into Hindsight retain
- No rewriting the vault from memories
- Research → wiki; prefs/decisions → Hindsight; agenda → `hot.md`
- Topic switch: `recall`, then `wiki/index.md` / search
- Wiki vs Hindsight conflict: cite both; don’t silently pick a side; file durable conflicts on the wiki page with `> [!contradiction]`
